data namespace_kernel_authority_amendment_note: String = "THE KERNEL BAR AS FIRST WRITTEN DEADLOCKED ITS OWN SUCCESSOR, and this amendment is the fix (operator ruling, 2026-08-01). The recut landed namespace-binding-kernel with a red_control ending 'no second place in the compiler makes that same decision' and a handback demanding 'evidence that nothing else decides the same question'. That bar cannot be met while the bootstrap seed keeps its own hand-written none/one/many mirror inside the v1 adapter, and that mirror cannot be deleted until generic emission carries the canonical carrier with its required bounds. But namespace-reference-derived-closure DEPENDS on the kernel. So on the day the recut merged, the next step was already unstartable for a reason that had nothing to do with what the next step needs: deriving candidate populations does not require the seed mirror to be gone, it requires the canonical decision to EXIST and be callable.\n\nTHE CUT IS AUTHORITY VERSUS RETIREMENT. Owning the canonical decision and removing every rival implementation of it are separate achievements with separate evidence, and fusing them made an acceptance bar that no amount of correct kernel work could satisfy. The kernel now owns being the one canonical authority; namespace-legacy-choice-retirement owns deleting the older mechanisms, and the seed mirror is named there as one of its rows. A new node was deliberately NOT minted: that node already reads 'delete every other way of deciding what a name means' and already inventories every remaining place that decides, so the mirror is a row it should always have carried, and minting a sibling would have been a second home for one concept.\n\nTHE ADAPTER IS NOT THEREBY BLESSED. It remains a declared scaffold with its dissolution trigger on its own carrier, counted and visible; moving WHERE its retirement is tracked does not lower what is owed. What changes is only that a temporary bootstrap realization no longer gates work that does not depend on it.\n\nTWO ACCEPTANCE SENTENCES WERE ALSO WRONG AND ARE CORRECTED HERE. The red_control said 'a malformed name refuses', but this boundary accepts occurrence identities and derives no name spelling at all, so it named a check no implementation executes — it now reads malformed occurrence TRANSPORT. And the bar now states the two refusals that distinguish a malformed supplied population from a real verdict: a candidate handed in the wrong role refuses distinctly from one that is absent, and the same declaration supplied twice refuses as malformed rather than counting as two. Only two DISTINCT declaration identities are ambiguity. Collapsing either of those into an ordinary verdict would let a defective candidate producer read as a legitimate naming answer, which is the state-space conflation this whole lane exists to remove."

data five_minute_ci_gate_program_note: String = "PROGRAM BOUNDARY, NOT A SINGLE PR (operator dispatch K, 2026-08-01; sequence revision eager-boar-610, 2026-08-01; contract re-anchored by operator ruling 2026-08-02). Product contract: every required operation performs the bare minimum computation needed to serve it — no recomputation of any semantic fact whose inputs did not change; wall-clock falls out of the realization/materialization goals rather than defining them. Five minutes is NOT the contract — it is the distress ceiling ('this is hard / not working well'), retained only as the Stage C checkpoint bound. Sub-lane roster, revised by the CI2-0 STOP (operator ruling 2026-08-10, superseding the 2026-08-08 CI-0 recut) — UNORDERED: dispatch order follows the graph edges, and THE NATIVE ROW NO LONGER PRECEDES THIS GATE. That edge is deleted, on a measurement rather than a preference: a 3,290s floor carries 97s of witness evaluation, so an infinitely fast evaluator leaves ~97 percent of the floor standing and native execution cannot be this gate's prerequisite. The one-PR CI-0 shape is retired with it — #8043/#8080 attempted it, the cohort was empty at the real frontier, and native-selected-witness-bundle is re-cut as the named self-host frontier it always was. The lanes: #7522 warm-merge-admission with net wall receipt; #7534 continued as materialization substrate under module-grain (hierarchy: module parse/type/interface → resolved entry → native bundle; no default CI savings until ordinary invocations consume it); union CLOSED per #7533 → per-entry-assembly narrow lane; this parent registration. Native-at-small-scale evidence has LANDED; operational migration rate remains OPEN with equivalence/fallback/identity/memory fail-closed. The landed change, its merge commit, the head the witnesses actually executed at, and the cited executing witness are execution evidence, not design criteria: they live in ONE typed receipt, gunbc.native_witness_transition_receipt native_at_small_scale_transition_receipt, and are restated neither here nor in gunbc.design_document (operator ruling on gunbc#7710, 2026-08-02 — this note and the design document previously carried independent hand-maintained copies of the same advancing status). Staged expectations (not flat 30–35min): Stage A modest admission saving only; Stage B first order-of-magnitude witness reduction after production native cutover; Stage C five-minute gate when all conjunction in docs/plans/five-minute-ci-gate-design.md holds. Dispositions: entry-graph-union CLOSED; retention PARKED (#7581). See docs/plans/five-minute-ci-gate-design.md."

// THE BROAD NAMESPACE NODE WAS TOO COARSE TO CLOSE HONESTLY, and the recut is the fix (operator
// ruling, 2026-07-31). namespace-canonical-binding previously combined two separable things in one
// boundary: working out which declarations a name can see, and calling one decision function on
// them. A check proving only the none/one/many decision could therefore have marked the whole node
// accepted while candidate derivation, reference-derived dependency closure, and the production
// changeover all remained unbuilt — an acceptance hazard, and the exact shape of rung inflation
// DESIGN 4b forbids, where a carrier named for the top rung occupies the bottom one.\n\nThree
// prerequisites now stand in front of it. namespace-binding-kernel owns the decision alone, on a
// candidate population SUPPLIED to it. namespace-reference-derived-closure owns structural
// exposure, authored order, the candidate index, exact reference-to-declaration binding, and the
// derived dependency edges. namespace-ambiguity-discharge settles the genuinely-many cases from
// real compilation. namespace-canonical-binding KEEPS ITS DURABLE IDENTITY and is now the final
// production changeover only, so historical links resolve and no identity is reused.\n\nWhy the
// split falls exactly there: dependency edges are a PROJECTION OF THE BINDING, not a second
// authored statement. A program that instead authored the missing edges by hand reached 400 of 771
// files at roughly one import per CI floor before it was stopped; the unresolved population was
// evidence that binding and module discovery are coupled at the wrong boundary, not a backlog to
// grind down.\n\nTHE CHANGEOVER AND ITS SUCCESSOR ARE DISJOINT, and an earlier revision of this
// recut broke that (review 45649). It retitled namespace-canonical-binding as 'switch the whole
// compiler over' with a boundary reading 'every place that resolves a name', which swallowed
// namespace-bound-only-consumers underneath it — that node's own boundary is type checking, call
// lookup, and argument-count checks reading the decided answer. Overlapping boundaries are the §2
// redundancy this document exists to remove, and they are worse on a roadmap than in code:
// completing the parent would already entail most of the child, so either the child can never be
// honestly accepted or the parent was silently read narrower than it was written. The cut is
// PRODUCER versus READER. The changeover node owns the sites that WORK OUT what a name refers to,
// and the deletion of the search-everything fallback behind them. Its successor owns the READERS of
// that answer and their obligation to stop on unresolved or ambiguous. Neither entails the other,
// and each can be accepted on its own evidence.\n\nONE EDGE WAS DELIBERATELY NOT CHANGED.
// pderive-source-slot-binding still depends on namespace-canonical-binding, which now means it
// waits for the whole production changeover. It plausibly needs only occurrence transport plus the
// binding kernel, but that is unproven: the dependency moves only once the focused P-derive
// consumer demonstrates it can operate on an exact supplied candidate population. Loosening it on
// the strength of the argument alone would be asserting a fact nobody has measured.

// THE RULE THAT ORDERS THE COMPUTE LANE, and it is a sequencing ruling rather than a design
// preference (operator, 2026-08-07): do not move the present arrangement onto our own machines.
// Move exact computations onto one shared fabric, and DELETE THE DUPLICATED WORK BEFORE increasing
// the number of things asking for it. Handing agents a build capability without deduplication and
// admission would not be a fabric — it would be a tidier way for ten callers to launch ten cold
// builds of one tree, which is the failure the lane exists to prevent. That is why
// compute-deduplication-and-admission stands in front of ci-owned-execution in the graph rather
// than beside it: owning CI adds a consumer, and a consumer added before the duplication is removed
// multiplies the load instead of sharing it.
//
// THE SECOND HALF OF THE SAME RULE APPLIES TO NATIVE EXECUTION. Emitting a native witness bundle
// and running it is the right destination, and the miniature is decisive at the scale it measures —
// direct native calls in single-digit milliseconds against tens interpreted and hundreds through
// warm cargo transport. But the cited production enrolment delivered zero of three native and three
// of three fallback, so the required path took no benefit from it, and native bodies surrounded by
// duplicated preparation would still be bad CI. Native realization and shared preparation are ONE
// programme, not two lanes competing for the same slot; native-selected-witness-bundle owns the
// first, and the discovery snapshot, scoped substrate, early selection and streaming rows own the
// second.
//
// WHY THE MECHANISM ROWS ARE A CHAIN AND NOT A SET. The measured floor is dominated by preparation
// rather than by the work being prepared for: on the clearest full-floor subject, the discovery
// batch spent the large majority of its wall on setup and resolve and a small minority actually
// evaluating witnesses, and the two workers walked the same roots twice. Each row therefore removes
// a DIFFERENT duplicate — the second walk, the second initialised world, preparation that precedes
// selection, and the barrier between preparing and executing — and each is only measurable once the
// one before it has landed. Chaining them with dependency edges is what keeps at most the next one
// startable, so the standing limit on concurrent performance mechanisms falls out of the graph
// rather than being restated as prose that nothing enforces. Width two is deliberately absent from
// that chain and stays parked: the tested implementation shared typed bytes while each worker still
// built its own world, and the architectural prerequisite is that no second private semantic world
// exists.

// THE PERMANENT PRODUCT INTERFACE IS TWO OPERATIONS (operator convergence mandate 2026-08-09):
// gunbc build <program> and gunbc test <program>. DEVBOOT, CI2, CONFIDENCE, CONVERGE,
// materialization and lenses are implementation responsibilities behind those operations, never
// separate user workflows — the caller never chooses runner, cache, affected-set algorithm,
// interpreter, bundle partition, realization provider, lease, ref, store, or host. #8049 owns gunbc
// build (the caller sees Built with program subject, artifact and receipt, or a typed refusal —
// never leases or refs); #8043 owns the reusable v2 test-plan execution behind gunbc test;
// V2-LENS-0 and dirty-worktree verification consume both. An incomplete affected-set answer selects
// the COMPLETE v2 test plan — never zero tests, never the interpreter. CI converges toward gunbc
// test with an exact tested-merge-tree subject: local-versus-CI becomes subject and policy, not
// separate architecture. Cross-process edge-index materialization is SUPPORTING WORK inside
// LENS-0/DEVBOOT, not a sixth program; before it builds, the remaining gates hold: attribute the
// un-decomposed resolve residue to its own seam, reproduce the cold misses in a fresh process,
// compare miss keys across at least two corpus subjects, prove no other in-process consumer
// reconstructs the value — then add a request family to the EXISTING materialization provider,
// never a parallel cache, and only after content-derived SourceFile identity lands (a deserialized
// index and a freshly built one must agree by construction). Artifact reuse identity stays pure and
// process-independent (content, environment, phase, policy, algorithm); producer and consumer
// process coordinates — invocation, host identity, boot identity, pid, process start identity,
// executable digest — live in production and consumption receipts and leases, extending DEVBOOT's
// existing lease and attempt vocabulary, never the artifact key.

// Every node below is ExecutionContractUnspecified: the declared, fail-closed migration frontier
// for gunbc.roadmap_execution_contract. A node states the exact validation operations that close it
// before the actuator will spawn for it, so dispatch refuses with a typed environment-admission
// diagnostic rather than guessing validations or dependencies. The prior binding lived on a
// pre-refresh operator-TODO node deleted by the 2026-07-27 authority refresh; re-binding is
// per-node roadmap authoring, never a merge-time default.

// THE FIRST BOUND NODE, and it is bound to an ALREADY-GREEN validation on purpose. Until this row
// existed every node was ExecutionContractUnspecified, so dispatch_environment_admit refused on all
// of them and no part of the workflow below Env had ever executed end to end. A first binding
// therefore has two jobs that pull in opposite directions: prove the Verify path runs at all, and
// prove it discriminates. Those want different nodes, and conflating them is how a green pipeline
// gets mistaken for a working one. This row takes the FIRST job only — the validation it names
// passes today, so an Agent turn that changes nothing still produces a real admitted environment, a
// real derived command, and a real validation receipt. What that proves is the PLUMBING: capability
// admission, argv derivation, and receipt production, independent of whether the provider
// accomplished anything. It deliberately proves NOTHING about discrimination, and must not be read
// as evidence that Verify can fail — the discriminating red belongs on a second node whose
// validation is currently red and goes green when the work lands, and that node is the next
// binding, not this one.
//
// The operation is the transport-clean corpus witness because it is what this ticket's own red
// control describes: 'a new unclassified production construction site reds the census'. It reads
// the live tree (SubstrateInputsOnly), so it is a statement about the repository rather than a
// fixture — a raw shell literal reappearing in that transport module reds it for real.

// THE BINDING NOW DISCRIMINATES, which is the half observation_raw_print_retirement_contract_note
// records this contract as deliberately not supplying. It named
// corpus_dag_compile_clean_transport_clean_holds -- an ALREADY-GREEN validation -- so Verify proved
// only that the path RUNS: admission, argv derivation, receipt production. A verifier that returned
// green unconditionally was indistinguishable from a working one, because nothing it ran could
// return anything else.
//
// This contract names a validation that WAS red until the node's work landed: the specimen's setup
// was then usb_gadget_setup_script (deleted by the change that described the transport), which
// prefixed "set -e" and joined rendered shell lines, so the witness asserting no shell control word
// was red, and the red was this node's own acceptance condition rather than a planted fixture: the
// node asks for a described operation instead of written shell text, and the witness asserts exactly
// that no shell text is produced. The transition red -> green WAS the work being finished, and it
// completed on 2026-09-29 -- the witness stays as the permanent regression control, so the red it
// would go now is exactly the regression it guards against.
//
// WHILE THE TEST WAS RED, the witness was enrolled in floor_expected_red, NOT
// QuarantineProbeExpectRed, and the difference was executional rather than stylistic. The sibling
// note above recommends the quarantine cadence,
// and that recommendation is STALE: std.witness_admission records that falsifier.yml -- the
// workflow scheduling QuarantineProbeExpectRed -- was deleted at 611fd02770 (#8283), so every row
// classified into that cadence "has read as covered ever since despite executing nowhere".
// Enrolling here would have put a deliberately-red acceptance test somewhere it never runs, which
// is the failure that note itself documents. The floor executes. When the test greened, the
// floor_expected_red row left by the roster's own removal path -- the counted un-quarantine, not a
// silent pass -- which is why nothing points there now.
fn shell_typed_invocation_execution_contract() -> WorkItemExecutionContract {
  gunbc_claim_execution_contract(
    entry: "dag/test/claim/shell/shell_typed_invocation_witness_test.dag" as FilePath,
    function: "usb_gadget_setup_emits_no_shell_control_word" as NonEmptyStr,
  )
}

data observation_raw_print_retirement_contract_note: String = "THE DISCRIMINATING BINDING — the half shell_typed_invocation_contract_note deliberately does not supply. That one names an already-green validation and therefore proves only that the Verify path RUNS: admission, argv derivation, receipt production. It cannot distinguish a working verifier from one that returns green unconditionally, because nothing it runs is capable of returning anything else. A pipeline with only that binding is the coverage-by-illusion tier — machinery present, nothing gating on it.\n\nThis contract names a validation that FAILS today. observation_emit_frontier_count() is non-zero -- the roster names which families remain, so no count is recited here, because a number written beside a fold is a second naming scheme and THIS ONE HAD ALREADY ROTTED: it read 8 while the typed dispositions summed to 7, and the 2026-09-11 restoration of the floor heartbeat is what made it stale; the witness asserts 0, which is this node's handback stated exactly ('the classified zero-residue progress census'). So Verify has a target that can genuinely go red, the red is the ticket's own acceptance condition rather than a planted fixture, and the transition red -> green IS the work being finished. Together the two bindings pin both directions: one proves the path executes, the other proves it discriminates, and neither claim is available from the other.\n\nThe witness is enrolled QuarantineProbeExpectRed in gunbc.ci_layer_roots so a deliberately-red acceptance test does not red the corpus — the cadence built for precisely this, where greening is a counted un-quarantine event and not a silent pass."

fn observation_raw_print_retirement_execution_contract() -> WorkItemExecutionContract {
  gunbc_claim_execution_contract(
    entry: "dag/test/claim/observation_raw_print_retirement_acceptance_test.dag" as FilePath,
    function: "observation_emit_frontier_is_zero" as NonEmptyStr,
  )
}

