data namespace_structural_observations_execution_contract_note: String = "BOUND (this change). The retracted interim below is answered rather than merely quoted: the closing validation now consumes admissions PRODUCED BY AN ORDINARY COMPILE OF ONE FILE and reaches its verdict through assess_reference_binding_observation, never through variant counting. Four StructuralBindingProductionRefused observations green nothing -- a production refusal assesses to ReferenceDerivedClosureRefused, which the set difference keeps in the frontier.\n\nWHAT THE BINDING ADDS BEYOND THE FOUR CAPABILITIES, and it is the half the retraction named as missing: SUBJECT PROVENANCE. Every admission carries the module path the parse itself declared, and the check refuses unless all of them name the one declared subject. Four admissions from four hand-built sources satisfy the capabilities and fail this check, which is exactly the difference between the row as written and the fixture suite that preceded it.\n\nWHAT THE VALIDATION EXECUTES: gunbc.namespace_structural_observations_production reaches the v1 parser walk through one hermetic host bridge (declared and enrolled seed growth, gunbc.namespace_structural_observation_bridge_seed_growth), so the witness declares SubstrateInputsOnly truthfully, runs in the required floor, and is not a member of the DeclinedLiveTree arm. Its four red controls are single-edit mutants of the one subject, each refusing exactly the capability whose rule the edit broke.\n\nRETRACTED INTERIM (2026-08-04, operator ruling via loyal-ram-550), kept because it is what this binding had to satisfy: the prior ordinary_compile_structural_closing_contract_holds predicate checked only scenario-variant presence and could green four StructuralBindingProductionRefused observations -- worse than no binding. STALE CITATION CORRECTED (2026-08-18, dead-witness-tree triage): the fixture it cited had no executing consumer since v1_claim_scoped_witness_batch was deleted 2026-08-15 and did not survive the triage; receipt at gunbc.ci_layer_roots v1_dead_witness_tree_triage_receipt."

fn namespace_structural_observations_execution_contract() -> WorkItemExecutionContract {
  gunbc_claim_execution_contract(
    entry: "dag/test/claim/namespace_structural_observations_acceptance_test.dag" as FilePath,
    function: "namespace_structural_observations_closing_contract_holds_on_one_ordinary_compiled_file" as NonEmptyStr,
  )
}

// THE SIX-ARM CLOSING DISCRIMINATOR for namespace-reference-derived-closure. The validation is
// deliberately RED while its production admission seam carries a typed unavailable row for every
// clause: the closed capability population is the node's own red control, and missing capabilities
// are a derived set difference, so duplicate evidence cannot hide an unexecuted clause and zero
// work cannot verify as complete. Clauses (a-d) wait on #7515's structural candidate producer, (e)
// waits on its reference-derived dependency projection, and (f) waits on the projection's
// pool-membership-independence wall. The paired fixture suite executes the merged P1 kernel for the
// first four clauses and proves every clause rejects its planted wrong output, but the bound
// acceptance witness imports none of those fixtures; it can green only when the gated node supplies
// production observations. It is enrolled QuarantineProbeExpectRed until that transition.

fn namespace_reference_derived_closure_execution_contract() -> WorkItemExecutionContract {
  gunbc_claim_execution_contract(
    entry: "dag/test/claim/namespace_reference_derived_closure_acceptance_test.dag" as FilePath,
    function: "witness_namespace_reference_derived_closure_closing_contract_holds" as NonEmptyStr,
  )
}

// THE CLOSING CHECK IS STRUCTURAL, NOT A POPULATION PIN, and that choice is the whole content of
// this binding. The node asks whether the interpreter's dispatch surface is ENUMERABLE and whether
// its roster can silently disagree with the dispatch; it does not ask how large the surface
// currently is. So the bound validation asserts properties that survive the roster legitimately
// growing -- named dispatch sites contribute derived rows, duplicate row keys refuse, shadows are
// exactly the known set BY NAME, every declared row carries its own dissolution trigger, an arm
// carrying no semantic primitive identity stays representable, and an unrecognised form label
// refuses rather than defaulting.
//
// Binding it to counts would have re-created at the acceptance layer the exact defect #7615 removed
// from the witness layer: the five deleted witnesses pinned live-population numbers copied from the
// tree, which DESIGN.md 5 rules is not an oracle, and they duly behaved as pure change detectors
// that redded main twice. A closing check that reds on legitimate growth is worse than one that
// does not exist, because it trains everyone to edit the number rather than read the change.
//
// The validation can genuinely fail: removing a dispatch site, dropping a declared row's trigger,
// admitting an unknown form label, or letting a second arm identity shadow a spelling each red it.
// The detectors' own discriminating REDs and positive controls live in
// test.claim.v1_interpreter_primitive_surface_witness_test and execute beside it.

fn v1_interpreter_primitive_roster_execution_contract() -> WorkItemExecutionContract {
  gunbc_claim_execution_contract(
    entry: "dag/test/claim/v1_interpreter_primitive_roster_acceptance_test.dag" as FilePath,
    function: "v1_interpreter_primitive_roster_acceptance_contract_holds" as NonEmptyStr,
  )
}

// THE CLOSING CHECK FOR v1-interpreter-primitive-dispatch-authority. R1 inverts the roster:
// gunbc.v1_interpreter_primitive_surface v1_interpreter_authored_roster_arms is the canonical
// authority as authored InterpreterPrimitiveDispatchArm rows; v1_interpreter_dispatch_emit derives
// Rust enum variant names from arm identity and generates lookup tables. Compile-time
// exhaustiveness is site-scoped: single-family dispatch sites get a non-wildcard enum match;
// eval_call_bridge and eval_call_native_intercept share one enum per site but expand per-family
// subsets with a required wildcard (missing handler body is runtime unreachable!, not compile error
// — per-family enum split is follow-up). Structural properties that survive roster growth are
// asserted here; R0 discriminating controls remain in
// v1_interpreter_primitive_surface_witness_test.

fn service_evidence_capture_execution_contract() -> WorkItemExecutionContract {
  gunbc_claim_execution_contract(
    entry: "dag/gunbc/roadmap/roadmap_service_evidence.dag" as FilePath,
    function: "service_evidence_capture_acceptance_holds" as NonEmptyStr,
  )
}

fn v1_interpreter_primitive_dispatch_authority_execution_contract() -> WorkItemExecutionContract {
  gunbc_claim_execution_contract(
    entry: "dag/test/claim/v1_interpreter_primitive_dispatch_authority_acceptance_test.dag" as FilePath,
    function: "v1_interpreter_primitive_dispatch_authority_acceptance_contract_holds" as NonEmptyStr,
  )
}

// THE SCM P1 CLOSING DISCRIMINATOR, authored only after the first P1 carrier made the node's whole
// completion condition executable. The validation is deliberately RED: its closed capability
// population is the roadmap node's own bar, and this first slice supplies only the bounded
// candidate-generation model check. Missing behavior is derived set difference, never a
// hand-maintained progress count; duplicate passing rows cannot erase it, and a false row remains
// missing. The contract therefore cannot green on zero progress and cannot confuse a modeled
// carrier with an executed proof kernel. It is enrolled QuarantineProbeExpectRed in
// gunbc.ci_layer_roots. Each later P1 slice adds an executing scenario check without weakening the
// aggregate. When the final capability greens, that same change removes the expect-red enrollment
// and promotes the witness to ordinary discovery ratchet.

// The per-node execution binding, shaped as a COMBINATOR rather than a parameter on every
// constructor (the `sign` twin below is the precedent, and it already carries `execution:
// rn.execution` through untouched). Threading an execution argument through
// active/active_small/active_large/authored/derivable/ticket_row would edit seven constructors and
// every one of their ~46 call sites to express a fact that today holds for exactly one node — the
// churn a combinator avoids, and the reason `sign` is a combinator too. A node without this wrapper
// keeps ExecutionContractUnspecified, which is the fail-closed refusal
// roadmap_execution_contract_frontier_note declares, not a default anyone chose.

// A BINDING NAMES THE VALIDATION THAT CLOSES A NODE, so it can only be authored once that
// validation exists. A node without one stays ExecutionContractUnspecified, which is the honest
// fail-closed state rather than a gap: dispatch refuses with a typed diagnostic instead of
// admitting an environment for work whose completion nothing can check. Fabricating contracts to
// make a lane look dispatchable produces exactly the coverage-by-illusion tier — every node
// clickable, every Verify vacuous. The closing validation is written as part of the node's first
// slice; the contract follows the witness, never precedes it.
//
// THE ROSTER IS NOT TRANSCRIBED HERE. This row previously carried a hand survey — 'two of six
// startable roots are bindable' plus the four names and why each lacked a validation — and it
// rotted exactly as a hand-maintained count must: two of the four it named
// (v1-test-hygiene-producer-retirement, pderive-typesafe-nullary-reflection) were accepted while
// the sentence still listed them as unbound, and the leading count was edited twice by unrelated
// changes. startable_nodes_missing_closing_contract() computes the same set from the nodes
// themselves, so read it there and delete nothing by hand. What stays here is the RULE, which does
// not change when the roster does.
//
// v1-test-migration records both sides of that rule: its false-green deletion-guard contract was
// removed, then a behavior-grain validation that can fail on zero progress was authored and bound.
// See v1_test_migration_binding_history_note for that history and v1_test_migration_contract_note
// for the current completion authority.

fn v2_emitter_producer_provenance_execution_contract() -> WorkItemExecutionContract {
  gunbc_claim_execution_contract(
    entry: "src/v2/test/claim/self_host/emitter_producer_provenance_witness_test.dag" as FilePath,
    function: "witness_restored_binding_without_executed_receipt_does_not_authorize_reds" as NonEmptyStr,
  )
}

// The validation is this node's red control stated almost verbatim. The ticket demands that 'a
// result recorded as made by the new generator, with no receipt from a run that actually produced
// it, has to be impossible to write', and
// witness_restored_binding_without_executed_receipt_does_not_authorize_reds asserts exactly that: a
// restored binding without an executed receipt does not authorize an emitter-produced claim. It is
// chosen over the suite's other twenty-six claims because it is the one that fails if the
// unrepresentability itself lapses, rather than one that checks a roster stayed in step.

// THE CANONICAL CLOSING VALIDATION for v2-emitter-direct-rust-door, bound to
// direct_rust_door_production_group_closing_expectation_holds — GREEN BY EXECUTION since
// 2026-09-06, when the known-red admission row deleted per its own dissolution ("every leaf
// reaches LeafEstablished by execution"), promoting the unchanged group root to the lane's
// permanent regression wall. The production walk is ingest → assemble → infer → emission on the
// real add_probe source and reaches ArtifactProduced: inference derives grounding for the whole
// specimen (declared-inhabitants roster membership, binding denotation, Conj/Arrow product
// introduction, canonical-operations and grammar-productions roster membership, and
// binding-reference derivation from the enclosing arrow's domain), and emission is the
// single-produced-declaration module composition (generate_rust_module_emission_candidate over
// v2.compiler.emit_produced), because a resolved module is a module shell over named
// declarations, never a type record to record-project. All five leaves establish: source
// fidelity byte-equal to direct_rust_door_expected_source, producer identity, seed-emitter
// absence, SourceProduced qualification, and the missing-rule refusal. State the walk claim
// exactly: ONE production implementation authority, ONE production walk per group construction,
// ONE scheduled group construction, measured by
// v2.test.claim.schedule_occurrence_multiplicity_test against the live falsifier schedule.
// Group ALGEBRA remains discriminated by planted-observation controls at zero production cost
// (v2.test.self_host.direct_rust_door_group_algebra). The group's observation is in-memory; the
// written-to-disk artifact surface is mint_written_provenanced_rust_artifact, which rides the
// same module composition.

fn v2_emitter_direct_rust_door_execution_contract() -> WorkItemExecutionContract {
  gunbc_claim_execution_contract(
    entry: "src/v2/test/claim/long/direct_rust_door_production_group_test.dag" as FilePath,
