// The validation names v1-seed-honesty-decision and executes the node's whole handback. Feeding one
// artifact identity as both claim and check refuses with bootstrap_self_verify_same_artifact;
// feeding separately identified artifacts with planted divergent content refuses with
// bootstrap_self_verify_diverged; mismatched source/compiler/hash-pin provenance refuses with
// bootstrap_self_verify_provenance_mismatch; separately identified artifacts with equal content and
// equal provenance admit, proving the refusals are discriminating rather than unconditional. The
// final conjunct requires seed_honesty_decision to carry one of the two operator verdicts whose
// rationale is NonEmptyStr by construction. That conjunct was SeedHonestyUndecided until
// 2026-08-02, so the closing validation was deliberately red and enrolled QuarantineProbeExpectRed
// and could not report done over the missing half; the operator verdict FixedPointTrustSufficient
// greened it and the enrollment was deleted in the same change (see
// v1_seed_honesty_decision_acceptance_note). The undecided pole did NOT retire with the quarantine:
// the conjunction is now a function of the decision, so
// seed_honesty_undecided_would_keep_closing_contract_red still executes it against
// SeedHonestyUndecided and reds if that arm is ever weakened. PRODUCTION-WIRING TRIGGER, STILL OPEN
// AND NOT DISCHARGED BY THE VERDICT: the realized-comparison and regen paths do not yet route their
// artifact identities through seed_self_verify_check. This contract proves the decision procedure
// and gates completion, but it is not yet the live trust-path authority. The verdict took the
// second branch of the choice this sentence set out -- fixed-point trust ruled sufficient -- and
// the rationale therefore disposes of the unwired path explicitly rather than implying it is
// protected, alongside the two other residuals it accepts (a fixed point does not defeat a
// self-reproducing defect; rollback is not fix-forward). Routing the realized artifacts through
// this check belongs to the generation-admission program, which is unbuilt. The full independent
// rebuild remains out of scope here.

// v1-test-migration WAS DELIBERATELY UNBOUND after its former binding to
// test_migration_delete_guard_holds was removed: that binding produced a false green, as reading
// what the guard actually computes showed.
//
// The guard is DIFF-SCOPED. cli_run.rs test_migration_delete_guard_uncovered_deletes_inner resolves
// a (base, head) pair, returns an empty violation list when base_rev == head_rev, returns an empty
// list again when neither rev resolves and GUNBC_CI_DIFF_BASE is unset, and otherwise inspects only
// the v1 test paths DELETED between those revs. Violations are empty whenever a change deletes no
// uncovered legacy test file, so the guard answers true. Measured on the tree that carried it: the
// guard passes today while test_migration_debt_live_module_count() is 81, so a dispatched agent
// could do no migration work at all and Verify would still go green. A validation that cannot fail
// on zero progress cannot close a node (DESIGN 5 — a wrong answer must be loud, and 'done' asserted
// over undone work is exactly the silent wrong answer).
//
// The guard was KEPT at the time this note was written, as a per-change deletion wall. IT IS NOW
// DELETED (2026-08-12, V1-CONSUMER-DRAIN-1): test_migration_delete_guard_holds,
// test_migration_delete_guard_uncovered_deletes and the whole guard body are gone from cli_run.rs,
// from the primitive registry, from the interpreter dispatch surface and from the v1 type env. The
// reason is not that the analysis above was wrong — it was right, and it is why the node was
// unbound — but that the guard's SUBJECT stopped existing: it authorized deletions by checking a
// stem against _retired.dag / _retained.dag carriers, and gunbc#8146 deleted every such carrier
// when the authority inverted from classifying departures to declaring residents. A per-change wall
// over an empty authorize-set refuses nothing. The deletion wall it provided is SUPERSEDED, not
// dropped: an undeclared or stale module now reds through the identity join in
// v2.lens.test_migration_debt retained_rust_kernel_wall_holds, which does not depend on anyone
// remembering to classify a departure. The paragraphs above are retained as the reasoning that
// unbound the node, not as a description of live code.
//
// The node's own bar — 'the per-file coverage mapping with nothing unmatched' — required a closing
// validation at the grain of legacy test BEHAVIOR, not modules: an admitted typed disposition for
// every discovered legacy test function, with unclassified as the derived set difference reaching
// zero. The module count is a trend metric that overstates debt by construction, because
// classification is exact-stem filename matching (chosen fail-closed after fuzzy matching wrongly
// reported an unrelated witness as covering `pipeline`), so a real witness under a different name
// still reads as debt. That missing graph once made the node honestly ClosingContractMissing in
// startable_nodes_missing_closing_contract. It now exists and the node is bound to it by
// v1_test_migration_execution_contract; v1_test_migration_contract_note records why that
// validation, rather than the deletion guard, is the completion authority.

fn v1_test_migration_execution_contract() -> WorkItemExecutionContract {
  gunbc_claim_execution_contract(
    entry: "src/v2/test/claim/manual/test_migration_debt_test.dag" as FilePath,
    function: "retained_rust_kernel_wall_holds_against_live_tree" as NonEmptyStr,
  )
}

// THE CLOSING CHECK FOR roadmap-receipt-continuity. Acceptance history is append-only JSONL carrier
// dag/gunbc/roadmap/roadmap_acceptance_event_history.jsonl; roadmap_acceptance_receipts is a replay
// projection only. Authored seal count/digest are deleted. Merge-base prior_history parses carrier
// content via git.Core.Show — never prior_history = [] on a changed carrier
// (PriorHistoryRevisionEvaluationRequired dissolved). The bound contract is the inhabitance leaf
// witness_deleted_history_event_refuses (a removed record with no withdrawal refuses). The other
// operator reds named in red_control — prefix law on non-empty observed prior, empty-prior bypass
// discriminant, digest-omitted field mutation, wrong prior digest, revocation while live, duplicate
// revocations, exact revocation admit, criteria rewrite, git-refusal observation, and typed
// load/projection refusal chain — are separate test fns in the same entry, discovered by the floor,
// not re-executed by this contract. Live git-observed integrity executes in
// test.claim.roadmap_receipt_continuity_live_witness (ReadsLiveTree, bin_witness_wet_entries).

// SHELL→DAG MIGRATION BATCH 1 execution contracts. The ten shell-dag-* nodes were authored
// without contracts, so launch admission refused them execution_contract_missing; these ten rows
// bind each one at authoring time. Each names a worker-authored witness file that does NOT exist
// yet — the dispatched worker authors it under its node's M0. Verification runs only after the
// worker commits, when the file exists; until then an unauthored witness fails verification as
// oracle-missing, which is the truthful outcome for work not yet done.

// REAL BINDING RESTORED 2026-09-20: the seeded red acceptance witness for this node has landed
