      line: ticket(t: fields(
        headline: "Record which generator actually produced each result",
        boundary: "Every result says which generator made it and how far it got, as two separate facts. Claiming the new generator made something, without the evidence that it did, has to be impossible to write down.",
        displaced_cost: "Right now everything is made by the old generator, and the count we track reads as if the new one made it. We are measuring the wrong thing, so we cannot tell how far along we are.",
        first_slice: "Relabel the existing rows as made by the old generator, and replace the single count with separate counts per generator in the same change.",
        red_control: "Where a file sits is not evidence of what made it: a result recorded as made by the new generator, with no receipt from a run that actually produced it, has to be impossible to write down rather than caught afterwards. Every row in the frontier roster is recorded as made by the old generator, because that is what made them — stated without a count on purpose, since the roster grows and a transcribed number goes stale (it read 'six' while the live roster held twenty-seven). Taking the old generator away proves nothing at this step, because nothing the new generator made exists yet — that check belongs to the two steps below, where there is finally something to compare.",
        out_of_scope: "Nothing changes which generator makes it here, and no check gets loosened to keep a number looking good.",
        handback: "The relabelled list, the retired count, and a demonstration that recording a result as made by the new generator, with no receipt from the run that made it, is refused outright rather than accepted and corrected later."
      )),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      execution: bound(contract: v2_emitter_producer_provenance_execution_contract()),
      parent: in_project(project: "v2-emitter-production", contribution: "Recording which generator made every result as a fact that cannot be claimed without its receipt is the lane's progress measure: the transition from old generator to new is countable, not asserted."),
    ),
