    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_7QVX2K4M9NBTR6HDJ0FZ8SWCPE",
      id: "v1-interpreter-primitive-roster",
      owner: "self-host",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/v1/v1_interpreter_primitive_surface.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: fields(
        headline: "Make the interpreter's primitive surface enumerable",
        boundary: "Every interpreter dispatch arm -- free call, method, guard-predicated bridge, native special and the one service carve-out -- has one interpreter-local identity, dispatch form and authored spelling, enumerable independently of semantic primitive identity. Adding or deleting an implementation arm without changing the roster refuses.",
        displaced_cost: "The interpreter's primitive surface had no roster anywhere, so nobody could ask which primitives it provides. That blocks the primitive-identity join at its fifth surface, and it blocks sequencing v1 deletion honestly: you cannot show nothing still needs a capability you cannot enumerate.",
        first_slice: "The roster is DERIVED FROM the dispatch. Each dispatch site in the seed expands its match arms and its roster rows from one macro token list, so the two cannot disagree; the sites that are not match arms at all stay declared, counted, each naming its own dissolution trigger. This node is mechanically preventive for the sites it covers and is explicitly NOT claimed as structural: the invalid state is unwritable within a site, but a whole new dispatch site can still be added in Rust without anyone noticing. Closing that is a separate node -- v1-interpreter-primitive-dispatch-authority -- which inverts the direction; this one is complete at the narrower bar and is accepted against it rather than being held open until the inversion lands.",
        red_control: "A dispatch arm added without a roster row, and a roster row with no arm, must both be unwritable rather than caught afterwards. A spelling reached by two different arms within one form is unreachable code and has to be named rather than silently accepted. A roster that cannot represent an arm carrying no semantic primitive identity fails this node outright, because that population is exactly what the identity join must discover.",
        out_of_scope: "Which semantic primitive each arm realizes belongs to the primitive-identity join, not here, and no row may carry an identity field. Generating the dispatch from the roster belongs to v1-interpreter-primitive-dispatch-authority. So does any claim that the Rust-side primitive denominator is closed: this node cannot make that claim and must not be read as making it.",
        handback: "The roster; three derived denominators -- dispatch sites, distinct arm identities, distinct authored spellings -- rather than one conflated count, each derived from the roster rather than pinned as a literal; row-grain enumeration provenance, since a row's provenance is a fact about that row and not about its dispatch form; a reconciliation of every quoted dispatch line in the seed file into either a row or a named non-primitive residue; a typed disposition for the Rust the scaffold adds, naming every symbol and the exact deletion condition; and witnesses whose exact assertions are grounded in named identities or controlled fixtures rather than in counts copied from the tree, each detector carrying both a discriminating red and a positive control."
      )),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      execution: bound(contract: v1_interpreter_primitive_roster_execution_contract()),
      parent: in_project(project: "v1-deletion-program", contribution: "Making the interpreter's primitive surface enumerable and derived from its dispatch is the denominator deletion must show empty: nothing can be proven unneeded if it cannot be listed."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_5PWQ9J3XZM8TKB2NHR6VD0FCAS",
      id: "v1-interpreter-primitive-dispatch-authority",
      owner: "self-host",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/v1/v1_interpreter_primitive_surface.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: updated(t: fields(
        headline: "Let the model, not the Rust, decide what primitives exist",
        boundary: "Invert the roster. Today the Rust dispatch is the authority and the roster is derived from it; here the roster becomes the authority and the interpreter's local arm identity and spelling/form lookup are GENERATED from it, leaving hand Rust to supply only the handler bodies behind an exhaustive match. The semantic question of which primitive an arm realizes stays a separate join and does not move here.",
        displaced_cost: "While the denominator lives in Rust, 'which primitives does the interpreter provide' can only be answered by reading Rust, and a new dispatch site added there is invisible to every consumer that asks. That keeps interpreter deletion a judgment call instead of a derived population, and it leaves the primitive-identity join reading a surface that can grow behind its back.",
        first_slice: "Generate the arm identity and the spelling/form lookup from the roster, and make the Rust handler match exhaustive over the generated identity — compile-time on single-family sites, runtime unreachable! backstop on bridge/native-intercept until per-family enum split.",
        red_control: "On single-family dispatch sites (eval_builtin_inner, eval_algebra_method_inner, try_v2_std_collection_map_primitive_grounding, try_parse_table_memo_dispatch), a roster row with no Rust handler must fail COMPILATION, not a test. On eval_call_bridge and eval_call_native_intercept — shared enums with per-family macro subsets — the same mismatch degrades to runtime unreachable! until per-family enum split lands (named follow-up). A Rust handler that is not reachable through a generated arm identity must not be addable as another string-dispatch path. Editing alias order or an authored spelling must not change an arm identity. One spelling under two different forms must stay representable. An accepted shape or arity is either modeled on the roster or typed as unknown -- never guessed. And no Rust-only spelling denominator may remain anywhere: if one does, this node is not done.",
        out_of_scope: "Semantic primitive identity, which stays with the identity join. Deleting the interpreter, which is downstream. Any widening of what counts as a primitive: this node changes who decides, not the population. Per-family enum split for bridge/native-intercept compile-time exhaustiveness is follow-up, not a blocker for this node's narrowed bar.",
        handback: "The generated identity and lookup; site-scoped exhaustive handler match — compile-time refusal on single-family sites (witnessed in interpreter_dispatch_authority.rs), runtime unreachable! backstop on bridge/native-intercept with per-family enum split named as follow-up; deletion of the R0 macro authorities, the roster functions and the interpreter_dispatch_arm_rows self-reading bridge; a stated disposition for each of the two declared R0 residual rows -- either moved into the authority or retained with its own independently justified non-primitive reason; and the hand-Rust line delta the inversion removes."
      ), on: "2026-09-30", note: "Awaiting the operator's acceptance event: v1_interpreter_primitive_dispatch_authority_acceptance_contract_holds (dag/test/claim/v1_interpreter_primitive_dispatch_authority_acceptance_test.dag); evidence #7682.")),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      execution: bound(contract: v1_interpreter_primitive_dispatch_authority_execution_contract()),
      parent: in_project(project: "v1-deletion-program", contribution: "Moving the primitive denominator from Rust into the model stops the roster growing behind every consumer's back, so the deletion frontier is a derived population rather than a judgment call."),
      centering: plan(text: "Run the named test process on dag/test/claim:v1_interpreter_primitive_dispatch_authority_acceptance_test. Confirm v1_interpreter_primitive_dispatch_authority_acceptance_contract_holds is green. Change nothing. Hand back the receipt. Stop if red or enrolled expect-red."),
    ),
