    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_7T6WSS1JYCV6GQNW1PZG73B0G3",
      id: "shell-typed-invocation",
      owner: "shell",
      carriers: carrier(path: "docs/plans/shell-to-dag-residual-census-and-arc-completion.md"),
      line: ticket(t: updated(t: fields(
        headline: "Describe what a command should do, instead of writing shell text",
        boundary: "Callers say which operation and which arguments; nobody hands over an opaque string of shell as the instruction.",
        displaced_cost: "Shell syntax embedded in decision-making code cannot be checked before it runs, and cannot be reused anywhere else.",
        first_slice: "Move the USB gadget configfs setup (extdeps.linux.usb_gadget: usb_gadget_setup_ops renders through configfs_op_line and usb_gadget_setup_script joins `set -e` and `|| true`) onto described operations: each ConfigfsOp becomes a typed command (extdeps.exec.command ArgvCommand or a typed filesystem write) with a typed refusal for bad arguments, and the string-building is DELETED, not stubbed to return an empty string. Two consumers must stay green by execution: the acceptance oracle dag/test/claim/shell/shell_typed_invocation_witness_test.dag (its function usb_gadget_setup_emits_no_shell_control_word is red today and turns green when no shell control word is rendered; re-point what it reads if the surface moves, never its name) and dag/test/claim/bmc/bmc_virtual_media_witness_test.dag, whose srv4 gadget tests assert what the setup produces and are migrated to the described form, not deleted.",
        red_control: "Bad arguments or an unavailable operation refuse before any shell is produced; the acceptance oracle refuses while `set -e`, `||`, `&&`, `;` or `2>/dev/null` appear in the rendered setup.",
        out_of_scope: "Genuinely shell-shaped leftovers stay in the shell layer. A function that returns an empty string in place of the deleted rendering is not a deletion; a `posix_sh_program_command` wrapping the old shell text is not a described operation.",
        handback: "The described version, both witness modules green by execution, and the deleted string-building."
      ), on: "2026-09-30", note: "Not yet centered: needs a centering plan: its ticket is the USB-gadget slice while it also heads the shell batch, so the slice and the project alignment must be split before a plan is written.")),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      execution: bound(contract: shell_typed_invocation_execution_contract()),
      parent: in_project(project: "dp-m2-shell-residue-retired", contribution: "The shell-typed-invocation batch is the first half of the shell-to-dag residue this milestone retires: replacing shell strings with described operations closes the largest uncheckable-invocation gap the corpus carries."),
    ),

    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_K7P3X9Q2MN8R6WTH5JVD4MCZ1G",
      id: "shell-dag-cron-entry-line-builder",
      owner: "shell",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/tools/cron_tag.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: fields(
        headline: "Build the cron entry line from typed intent, not string concat",
        boundary: "gunbc.tools.cron_tag build_cron_entry_line routes its fields (schedule, command, tag) through a typed cron-entry intent realized by the bash-grammar rows of v2.workflow.orchestration_bash_emit_support, never by concatenation. Cron stays the foreign executor and the emitted line stays a crontab line — the change is who decides its bytes.",
        displaced_cost: "A crontab line assembled by concat in decision code cannot be checked before cron runs it — a quoting or metacharacter defect detonates inside the scheduler, not at the refusal — and the entry shape cannot be reused by any other scheduler-facing surface.",
        first_slice: "The acceptance witness dag/test/claim/shell/shell_dag_cron_entry_line_builder_witness_test.dag is authored, pinned at launch, and RED. Do NOT edit it — an edit refuses verification as oracle-moved. Make it green by doing M1-M3. M1: model the typed entry intent over the existing grammar rows, following v2.workflow.orchestration_bash_emit_support. M2: rebind build_cron_entry_line onto the intent and DELETE the concat — not stubbed to return an empty string. M3: witness green by execution.",
        red_control: "The rendered entry line contains no shell control word (set -e, ||, &&, ;, 2>/dev/null); a typed-form control asserts the entry is built from declared schedule/command/tag fields; a malformed field refuses before any line is produced.",
        out_of_scope: "Cron remains the executor and a crontab line remains genuinely shell-shaped output. A posix_sh_program_command wrapping the old concatenated text is not a described operation; an empty-string stub is not a deletion.",
        handback: "The described builder, the deleted concat, and the witness green by execution on the named test process."
      )),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      execution: bound(contract: shell_dag_cron_entry_line_builder_execution_contract()),
      parent: in_project(project: "shell-typed-invocation", contribution: "Shows the pattern on the smallest surface: one rendered line derived from typed intent, proving callers can name operations instead of shell text."),
      centering: plan(text: "Target: dag/gunbc/tools/cron_tag.dag, symbol build_cron_entry_line. Exemplar: shell-typed-invocation. (1) The acceptance witness dag/test/claim/shell/shell_dag_cron_entry_line_builder_witness_test.dag is authored, pinned at launch, and RED. Do NOT edit it — an edit refuses verification as oracle-moved. Make it green by doing M1-M3. (2) Move the concat onto a typed cron-entry intent realized through the bash-grammar rows of v2.workflow.orchestration_bash_emit_support — the precedent the node row names; do NOT author a second grammar. (3) Row edit: rebind build_cron_entry_line onto the intent and delete the concat; no empty-string stub, no posix_sh_program_command around the old text. (4) Acceptance: the named test process, pattern //dag/test/claim/shell:all. Pitfall: cron is a foreign executor — the emitted line stays shell-shaped; only its construction moves."),
    ),
    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_Q8F2R5L9BN4X7WPK3HJD6MCZTG",
