        boundary: "The ci_floor_peak_*_command rows of v2.workflow.ci_floor_peak_emit — the echo/sed/2>/dev/null rows the module's own Phase-2 note names — are replaced by typed filesystem observation leaves; the consumers of those rows read typed values, never rendered shell.",
        displaced_cost: "Each calibration row is shell text authored inside a decision fold and handed to the runner as an opaque string: a bad path or a metacharacter is invisible until the runner executes it, and 2>/dev/null swallows exactly the absence the calibration needs to refuse on.",
        first_slice: "The acceptance witness dag/test/claim/shell/shell_dag_floor_peak_calibration_rows_witness_test.dag is authored, pinned at launch, and RED. Do NOT edit it — an edit refuses verification as oracle-moved. Make it green by doing M1-M3. M1: model the calibration readings as typed filesystem observation leaves per the module's own Phase-2 declaration. M2: rebind every ci_floor_peak_*_command row and its consumers to the typed leaves and delete the echo-row text. M3: witness green by execution.",
        red_control: "No rendered calibration surface carries set -e, ||, &&, ; or 2>/dev/null; a positive control asserts the typed observation leaves resolve on a planted fixture; a missing observed file refuses with a typed cause instead of an empty reading.",
        out_of_scope: "The runner-facing workflow may still receive shell for genuinely foreign steps; a posix_sh_program_command wrapping the old rows is not a described operation.",
