      line: ticket(t: fields(
        headline: "Replace the deploy thin-invoke `ROOT=$(git rev-parse || pwd)` with typed git.Core.ShowToplevel",
        boundary: "gunbc.ci_spec gunbc_ci_deploy_invoke stops deriving its ROOT prelude with ROOT=$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel || pwd) and reads the toplevel through typed git.Core.ShowToplevel with a nonzero-refuse arm. The `|| pwd` is an absorbing fallback (DESIGN §5: degradation disguised as fail-open) and is deleted, not preserved.",
        displaced_cost: "When git rev-parse fails, the fallback silently substitutes the working directory as the repo root — every later deploy step then acts on the wrong tree with no diagnostic, the exact absorbing-fallback failure: nothing is missed, nothing is reported, the wrong thing deploys.",
        first_slice: "The acceptance witness dag/test/claim/shell/shell_dag_ci_deploy_invoke_prelude_witness_test.dag is authored, pinned at launch, and RED. Do NOT edit it — an edit refuses verification as oracle-moved. Make it green by doing M1-M3. M1: bind the toplevel read to git.Core.ShowToplevel with a typed refusal on nonzero exit. M2: rebind gunbc_ci_deploy_invoke and delete the fallback spelling. M3: witness green by execution.",
        red_control: "The rendered invoke carries no || fallback and no shell control word; a positive control asserts the typed ShowToplevel read; a nonzero git exit refuses with a typed cause instead of substituting pwd.",
        out_of_scope: "The rest of the deploy thin-invoke stays as is; a posix_sh_program_command wrapping the old prelude is not a described operation.",
        handback: "The typed toplevel read, the deleted fallback, witness green by execution."
      )),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      execution: bound(contract: shell_dag_ci_deploy_invoke_prelude_execution_contract()),
      parent: in_project(project: "shell-typed-invocation", contribution: "Moves the deploy invocation prelude onto described operations, so the riskiest CI call is checkable before it runs."),
