    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_4XK7P2WQ9BNF6RTH3VJD8MCZ5L",
      id: "gate-refusal-reason-survives-wrapper",
      owner: "shell",
      carriers: carrier(path: "docs/plans/shell-to-dag-residual-census-and-arc-completion.md"),
      line: ticket(t: updated(t: fields(
        headline: "A gate's typed refusal reason survives the wrapper that reports it",
        boundary: "A wrapper that reports whether a gate passed carries the gate's reason with it. Collapsing a typed outcome to yes-or-no at the wrapper boundary is the defect, wherever the wrapper lives.",
        displaced_cost: "The gate already produces the reason and the wrapper discards it, so a consumer asking WHY a gate refused has to go back to the logs, and a ledger built on the wrapper cannot tell a subject refusal from an infrastructure failure. gunbc#11342 addresses exactly this shape one layer down -- an ExitFailure that collapses into a fabricated not-executed row -- and leaves the wrapper boundary standing.",
        first_slice: "emit_host_gate_passes reduces exit_ok(...) to a Bool; dissolve that collapse so the typed outcome std.process already carries reaches the gate's wrapper consumers. tools.emit_host_gate emit_host_verdict_narration_scaffold shells out a per-smoke verdict line ONLY because this wrapper discards ProcessExit.reason, and its dissolve-on fires when the claim path carries typed refusal reasons to the executor surface -- which gunbc#11342 does, and that PR deletes the scaffold and its trigger together. Either way this row's subject is untouched: the narration is the compensation, the wrapper collapse is the cause, and dissolving the compensation removes the marker without removing the collapse. That is why the collapse needs a home that does not depend on the marker surviving.",
        red_control: "A wrapper that reduces a typed outcome to a Bool is flagged, and a consumer asserting on the reason goes red when the collapse is reintroduced.",
        out_of_scope: "The accounting of hand-written shell sites, which is shell-residue-zero's subject; this row is about the typed outcome, not the shell that produced it.",
        handback: "No wrapper in the gate surface reduces a typed outcome to a Bool, with a consumer reading the reason green by execution. The handback is the collapse itself rather than a dissolution receipt, because the narration that compensated for it is retired by the same capability under DESIGN.md §4b(4) and cannot stand as evidence that the cause was addressed."
      ), on: "2026-09-30", note: "Not yet centered: needs a centering plan: no plan has been authored for this instance of bool_projection_over_a_typed_carrier.")),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
