    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_G2BR1NCSAD24KP0TA14TA89PMV",
      id: "serving-liveness-route-withdrawal",
      owner: "fleet",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/serving/serving_availability.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: updated(t: fields(
        headline: "A serving route that has stopped serving stops being routable, and the seats held against it are freed",
        boundary: "Whether a route can take new work is one reading, bound to the endpoint process that answered it, and every consumer projects from that reading rather than deciding separately. The reading covers three ways a route stops serving: the front door does not answer inside a bounded deadline; the endpoint process was replaced between observations; and the engine core is no longer advancing while requests are admitted. Seats and grants held against a launch that is gone become unusable rather than waiting out their term.",
        displaced_cost: "Group A was dark for 43 hours in September 2026 and nothing in the repository could say so: the health probes had no deadline, so a wedged engine held the roster gate, dispatch selection and placement open with no refusal, and one harness POST was held open for over thirty minutes against a backend that would never answer. A stalled engine still answers its front door, so the route stayed offerable throughout.",
        first_slice: "Cut 1 (merged): bounded probes with a caller-owned deadline, one sealed front-door availability verdict bracketed by two endpoint-process readings, endpoint-process continuity as its own sealed verdict for the seat fence, and model admission kept separate from availability. Cut 2: the engine-progress reading — the generation counter compared as exported text under one exporter, beside the running gauge, over an interval longer than a declared step bound — withholding a route only on an established stall. Cut 3: seats held against a replaced or stalled launch invalidated rather than held to term.",
        red_control: "An idle engine is not a stalled one: a motionless counter with nothing running is healthy however long it stands still, and calling it a stall evicts a working route. An interval shorter than one uninterruptible step establishes nothing and must read unread rather than stall. A restarted exporter resets its counters, so stillness or an apparent decrease across a replacement is unread. An unread progress reading is never a wall. A progress reading does not establish that the engine core behind the exporter is the same core, which remains the declared exporter-grain rung drop.",
        out_of_scope: "Cut 1 does not bound a POST already in flight, and a successful preflight read cannot: the request deadline belongs to the workload. Detecting a stall inside a running turn, which needs the endpoint on the turn configuration, is a later slice. Nothing here identifies the engine-core incarnation behind the exporter.",
        handback: "A route that does not answer, whose exporter was replaced, or whose engine has stopped advancing is refused as a placement candidate with a typed located reason and a countable refusal; seats held against a launch that is gone are released; and each refusal has a discriminating control that goes red when the rule is removed."
      ), on: "2026-09-30", note: "Not yet centered: needs a centering plan: Cut 2 (the engine-progress reading in gunbc.serving.serving_availability) has no plan yet.")),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "vm-service", contribution: "Work must not be routed to an inference endpoint that stopped serving; one bounded liveness reading withdraws the route and frees its seats."),
    ),




    roadmap_node(
