        headline: "Refuse a claim that is computed and thrown away",
        boundary: "Inside a function returning Bool, a bare Boolean expression in non-terminal position is censused and then refused. Its value cannot be observed, so computing one is either a mistake or a claim someone believes is being enforced.",
        displaced_cost: "Two independent keystones reported green while claims sat above the returned expression, discarded. One of them was a bob that could not settle. The defect is invisible at review because the discarded line reads exactly like an enforced one.",
        first_slice: "Census the corpus for the shape and report the population before refusing anything, because the size of it decides whether the wall lands in one step or behind a frozen roster.",
        red_control: "A planted discarded claim reds; a terminal Boolean expression and a Boolean bound by a let and later used both stay accepted, so the wall does not fire on legitimate code.",
        out_of_scope: "Not a general unused-expression rule, and no motion, capability or browser work belongs in this lane.",
        handback: "Return the census, the wall or the frozen roster with its dissolution trigger, and both controls."
      ), on: "2026-09-30", note: "Not yet centered: scope.")),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
      parent: in_project(project: "compiler-guarantee", contribution: "A claim computed and thrown away refuses."),
    ),
