      line: ticket(t: level_fields(
          headline: "The compiler refuses what a compiler must refuse, and says how sure it is",
          boundary: "The guarantee ladder's measurement (schema, probe corpus, claims carrier), the ordinary-floor walls (calls, methods, conformance, records, exhaustiveness, parse formation, generic fields), and the acceptance door that makes the floor blocking. Measured on the compiler the floor runs today, which is the v1 seed under gunbc.v1_maintenance_standing, and on v2 where a v2 twin exists.",
          approach: "Measure, then wall class by class, then flip the floor to blocking (accepted-floor-obligation-closure). The extended classes wait until the floor closes.",
          red_control: "Any floor class whose reported rung exceeds its executed evidence (§4b(1) rung inflation) keeps this red.",
          displaced_cost: "Without a measured floor, \"the compiler accepted it\" says nothing. Wrong programs are caught late, in rustc or in production.",
          handback: "accepted-floor-obligation-closure accepted, with the ladder census re-derived from receipts."
        )),
      parent: in_project(project: "v2-compiler-live", contribution: "The compiler that goes live must hold the ordinary floor (DESIGN §4b). A self-hosted compiler that accepts wrong programs only makes those wrong programs cheaper to produce."),
    ),
