      line: ticket(t: fields(
        headline: "NUMERIC-BIT cut 2: Width32/Width64 kernel arms in the interpreter and the emitter",
        boundary: "The bit operations over the sealed carrier at machine widths 32 and 64 realized as kernel arms in the v1 interpreter and in the Rust emitter, with one differential witness proving both targets agree on a discriminating corpus.",
        displaced_cost: "SHA-256 and every rotate-heavy primitive run as interpreted folds over Int, which is the cost that gates CRYPTO-0's landing.",
        first_slice: "FIRST the §3 fork: gunbc#11645 landed std.bitwise (word32_* over Int) beside std.machine_word in the same window -- two bit-operation authorities on main. Consolidate onto one before any kernel arm, then interpreter arms for the four rotate/shift/mask operations at Width32, the emitter twin, the differential witness.",
