    roadmap_node(
      identity: "rn_SYXHP92KEGX92XNFBZRXBQW2BV",
      id: "egress-crypto-0-sha256-landing",
      owner: "primitive-egress",
      carriers: carrier(path: "docs/plans/demand-engine-program.md"),
      line: ticket(t: updated(t: fields(
        headline: "CRYPTO-0: after the HMAC landing -- the native receipt instrument and the cost of interpreted SHA-256",
        boundary: "SHA-256 landed on main as extdeps.crypto.sha2 over std.bitwise (gunbc#11645). HMAC-SHA-256 over it, utf8_encode_octets, and the deletion of the hmac interpreter primitives, crate and evidence rows were reconciled in gunbc#11895 and SPLIT OUT of its landing (operator ruling 2026-09-21): under the honest floor their witnesses run at 0.8-1.4M eval steps against the 100ms-equivalent new-witness budget, so they wait on the kernel arms. Also owed with that landing: the 4b(3) declared drop for the constant-time tag comparison that verify_slice realized mechanically and hmac_tag_difference cannot observe (review 69492).",
        displaced_cost: "Without the instrument the .dag hash has no native receipt, and without the cost measurement the kernel-arms row is scheduled on a guess.",
        first_slice: "Re-draft the HMAC landing from gunbc#11895 at its immutable quarry head 8fc4448575cd4955c2b3b6c34ac6e300f41d31f1 (tag quarry/11895) once egress-numeric-bit-kernel-arms brings interpreted SHA-256 inside the floor budget; the constant-time rung-drop row lands with it.",
        red_control: "The native instrument refuses on a wrong label rather than reporting pass; a mutated round constant reds the FIPS 180-4 vectors in sha256_fips_witness_test.",
        out_of_scope: "SHA-384/512, P-256 and ES256 are the next row.",
        handback: "Return the instrument row and the measured cost."
      ), on: "2026-09-21", note: "Moved from the brief at the 100-word re-cut (context, not an obligation): The reconciled tree is gunbc#11895 at its immutable quarry head 8fc4448575cd4955c2b3b6c34ac6e300f41d31f1 (tag quarry/11895); #11895 is a quarry and never lands.")),
      dispatch: dispatchable(),
