      id: "required-floor-passes-with-a-failed-phase",
      owner: "ci-control",
      carriers: carrier(path: "dag/gunbc/witness/witness_floor_workflow.dag"),
      line: ticket(t: fields(
        headline: "A required run that had a phase fail must not report success",
        boundary: "When the required run reports how many phases it ran and how many failed, a nonzero failure count has to reach the verdict and the check result. Today it does not.",
        displaced_cost: "Observed on a live pull request: the job log recorded two phases run and one failed, with two located findings, while the same run reported a clean verdict and the check concluded success and the branch read as mergeable. A gate that passes while one of its phases failed certifies less than everyone reading it believes, and the belief is the point of having it.",
        first_slice: "Make the failed-phase count decide the verdict, then confirm on the run that already exhibits it.",
        red_control: "A run with a deliberately failed phase reports failure; a run with none still reports success, so the change does not simply make the gate refuse everything.",
        out_of_scope: "Not the content of any particular phase's findings, and not which phases the required run should contain.",
