        boundary: "std.interface_summary typed_module_key consumes a compiler identity it does not author, and its realization today is v1_compiler.closure_identity transform_content_digest -- the content hash of the RUNNING BINARY. src/v1/stage0/build.rs embeds GUNBC_BUILD_IDENTITY, the checkout's commit, into that binary through cargo:rustc-env, so a rebuild at ANY new commit re-keys every entry, including a corpus-only .dag commit. Derive the identity from what the TYPECHECKER actually is instead.",
        displaced_cost: "Every cross-push reuse claim in the materialization design depends on this and none of it is reachable without it. The store as landed delivers same-build cross-process reuse only, and that limit is a property of this derivation rather than of the store.",
