// AN EDGE HOLDS A CHILD UNTIL ITS PARENT HAS AN ACCEPTANCE RECEIPT, so a parent is chosen for what
// it OWES, never for what it historically preceded. `roadmap_program_view` puts a node in
// ObligationDependencyHeld for every declared parent lacking a receipt, which is why
// `2-scm-native-write-spine-acceptance` declares none: its only prerequisite was gunbc#10729
// landing, a landed change is not a roadmap node, and the nearest node that WOULD carry it,
// `2-scm-native-authority-program`, still owes the CAS slot consumers, the Git import wall and the
// bridge cutover. Edging to it would hold an executable row behind an entire unfinished program --
// the wrong dependency, made machine-readable, which is worse than the prose it replaced. Found by
// external review after the edge was added on exactly that reasoning.
// Shell→dag migration batch 1 edges: each node is a child of the completed exemplar
// shell-typed-invocation; the two same-file pairs (ci-deploy-invoke-prelude/ci-heal-regen-invoke,
// live-deploy-install-owned/live-deploy-restart-tailscale) carry NO edge between them — they are
// independent edits whose staggering constraint is a dispatch-scheduling fact recorded in their
// centering plans, not a dependency, and the graph has no exclusion-edge vocabulary.
