// Both digests below moved on 2026-07-29 because every row was rewritten in plain language, and the
// digest covers the brief, the pass/fail test, and what gets handed back. Worth being blunt about
// the limit this exposes: the digest cannot tell a rewording from a genuine change to the bar — it
// only knows the words moved. Nothing about what these two rows had to prove changed, and the
// evidence each names is the same run and the same files as before, so re-pinning is correct here.
// But that judgement was a person's, not the mechanism's, and a reviewer should treat any digest
// change as a prompt to re-read the row rather than as a formality. This is the same gap
// roadmap_acceptance_receipt_note already names: until a row's pass/fail test points at the test
// that discharges it, the link between words and evidence is asserted rather than derived.

