// supplied-candidate binding kernel, so the IMPLEMENTATION dependency for
// namespace-reference-derived-closure was resolved, but no acceptance receipt existed — leaving the
// roadmap saying its own prerequisite was unaccepted while the code depended on it. Two different
// truths for the same fact, which is exactly what node_is_startable reads, so P2a was being worked
// on while not honestly startable under the roadmap's own definition. The digest 2eba4715cdef42eb
// is the POST-#7530 value: #7530 rewrote this node's boundary, red_control and out_of_scope to cut
// authority from retirement, and roadmap_criteria_digest covers brief plus red_control plus
// handback, so the pre-amendment digest is stale by construction. It was DERIVED BY EXECUTION
// rather than transcribed — node_criteria_digest was run against the live node on this tree, not
// copied from a prior receipt or computed by hand. The red control names the malformed-transport
// refusal because that is the first arm #7530's amended row requires; the sibling arms (absent
// versus wrong-role identity distinct, duplicate supplied identity refused, wrong-category
